From: Gilly <gilroyscott1970@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: fix off-by-one in airoha_tc_remove_htb_queue

Backport of Lorenzo Bianconi's net patch (v2 1/2) "net: airoha: Fix
off-by-one in airoha_tc_remove_htb_queue".

airoha_tc_htb_alloc_leaf_queue() programs the per-channel TX rate limit
with the channel index, but the removal path called
airoha_qdma_set_tx_rate_limit() with queue + 1. Tearing down an HTB leaf
therefore cleared the rate limit on the wrong channel and left the
intended channel's limit stale. Pass queue, matching the allocation.

Only exercised when tc HTB hardware-offload (e.g. offloaded SQM) is in
use; harmless otherwise.
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
index 64dde6464f3f..aa98d1823ab6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3006,7 +3006,7 @@ static void airoha_tc_remove_htb_queue(struct net_device *netdev, int queue)
 	struct airoha_qdma *qdma = dev->qdma;
 
 	netif_set_real_num_tx_queues(netdev, netdev->real_num_tx_queues - 1);
-	airoha_qdma_set_tx_rate_limit(netdev, queue + 1, 0, 0);
+	airoha_qdma_set_tx_rate_limit(netdev, queue, 0, 0);
 
 	clear_bit(queue, qdma->qos_channel_map);
 	clear_bit(queue, dev->qos_sq_bmap);
